<title>USA: CSS Industries Q1 diluted shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>CSS Industries Q1 diluted shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(unaudited)</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							    March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	   1996</p>
<p> SALES					     $ 44,244    $ 47,270</p>
<p>COSTS AND EXPENSES</p>
<p>   Cost of sales				   25,022	27,488</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>    administrative expenses		    23,696	21,901</p>
<p>   Interest expense, net			  1,100	 1,499</p>
<p>   Rental and other income, net		 (595)	 (236)</p>
<p>							 49,223	50,652</p>
<p>LOSS BEFORE INCOME TAXES AND</p>
<p>  MINORITY INTEREST			     (4,979)     (3,382)</p>
<p> INCOME TAX BENEFIT			     (2,007)     (1,415)</p>
<p> LOSS BEFORE MINORITY INTEREST		(2,972)     (1,967)</p>
<p>MINORITY INTEREST IN INCOME OF</p>
<p>  SUBSIDIARIES, NET				   176	   118</p>
<p> NET LOSS					   (3,148)     (2,085)</p>
<p>NET LOSS PER COMMON SHARE</p>
<p>  Primary					     (.29)	 (.19)</p>
<p>  Fully diluted				     (.29)	 (.19)</p>
<p>WEIGHTED AVERAGE SHARES OUTSTANDING</p>
<p>  Primary					    10,805	10,954</p>
<p>  Fully diluted				    10,805	11,001</p>
<p>		     (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: In the first quarter of 1997, the company sold the U.K. and French operations of its affiliate Rapidforms Inc, and the company's subsidiary, Paper Magic Group Inc, acquired Color Clings Inc. Net of the acquisition and divestiture sales, sales decreased nine percent and the net loss increased 15 percent from 1996.</p>
<p>The increased loss for the first quarter was primarily attributed to the incremental seasonal losses of Color Clings and the timing of Easter shipments compared to a year ago.</p>
